 "help": "usage: wgsextract qc roh [-h] --af-file FILE [--af-tag TAG] [--af-build {hg19,hg38,t2t}]\n                         [--af-release TEXT] [--sample NAME] [--build {hg19,hg38,t2t}]\n                         [--regions REGIONS] [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --af-file FILE        Local population allele frequencies on the sample's build: a gnomAD/1000\n                        Genomes sites VCF/BCF or a bcftools roh table\n  --af-tag TAG          INFO field of --af-file holding the frequency, e.g. AF_nfe (default: AF)\n  --af-build {hg19,hg38,t2t}\n                        Build of --af-file, when its header doesn't give contig lengths\n  --af-release TEXT     Release of --af-file to record, e.g. 'gnomAD v4.1 genomes'\n  --sample NAME         The sample of a multi-sample VCF\n  --build {hg19,hg38,t2t}\n                        The input's build, when its header doesn't tell\n  --regions REGIONS     Assessed scope: comma-separated autosomes or ranges, e.g. chr20 or\n                        chr15:20000000-30000000 (default: every autosome in the header)\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n4 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract qc roh --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract qc roh --input sample.vcf.gz --af-file gnomad.genomes.v4.1.sites.chr15.vcf.bgz --regions chr15\n  wgsextract qc roh --input sample.vcf.gz --af-file 1kgp_af.vcf.gz --af-tag EUR_AF\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <stem>.roh.tsv (runs), <stem>.roh.json (wgsextract.roh/1: evidence, scope,\n  F_ROH, isodisomy review flags, provenance) and <stem>.roh.markers.tsv.gz.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, bgzip, tabix; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
